271:{character:player} Ichihime, as the priestess of Mahjong Soul Shrine, do you know anything about the famed tournament?
272:{character:Ichihime} Of course, nyaa! It's the tournament where the winners can make a wish to the master of the shrine, nyaa! Even the little children in One Han City know this, how could I not?
273:{character:player} Then could you be a little bit more specific?
274:{character:Ichihime} How could I know before the tournament begins? They'll only publish the rules once it starts. Master's being very weird today, nyaa.
275:{character:player} Eh? I thought that someone who works at the Mahjong Soul Shrine like you would know the process in advance?
276:{character:Ichihime} No way, nyaa! Each tournament has different rules. We only know what they are once it kicks off.
277:{character:player} Alright, so how about last time?
278:{character:Ichihime} Last time... Last time... What was it? How strange, I should know that...
279:{character:player} Let's talk about something else. Do you know the Four Great Jyanshis?
280:{character:Ichihime} Well, yes, but not that well. nyaa!
281:{character:???} Knows them, but not well, hee-hee...
282:{character:Kaguyahime} Why ask midget over there, when you could ask me? For you, {var:player_nickname}, there's nothing I wouldn't tell you!
283:{character:Ichihime} Oh! You again! Bad rabbit!
284:{character:Kaguyahime} I was just wondering why I hadn't seen midget at the shrine recently, and now I know! Gone to the café, eh...
285:{character:Ichihime} And what of it? It's nothing to do with you anyway, nyaa!
286:{character:Kaguyahime} Oh midget, seeing as you like the café so much, why don't I help you by taking over the Mahjong Soul Shrine? After all, however you look at it, it's much more appropriate for someone of my status to be in charge. Just think about it, eh? Hee-hee...
287:{character:Ichihime} Not a chance, nyaa!
288:{character:player} Haha, let's put a pin in that. Why don't you tell me about the Four Great Jyanshis, more importantly, Kaguyahime?
289:{character:Ichihime} Be careful, Master! Bad rabbit is a liar, nyaa!
290:{character:Kaguyahime} Tsk-tsk, I have never deceived you. Not. Once.
291:{character:player} ...That's a lie itself.
292:{character:Kaguyahime} Ehh, you mortals are so vexing, always questioning the gods. Be that as it may, shall we play a game? Should you win, I will tell you nothing but the truth. But should you lose, hee-hee, I say nothing at all!
293:{character:player} No harm in trying... What do you want to play?
294:{character:Kaguyahime} There's nothing particularly convenient to play at the moment, but isn't it lucky I happen to have a few Mahjong tiles on me... Hmm, let me see... Now, who will be today's big loser? Okay, we've got Red and White.
295:{character:player} Now what?
296:{character:Kaguyahime} I'm going to move them randomly, and your task is to pick one. If you choose Red, I shall tell you a tidbit about the Four Greats... And, seeing as you're on good terms with Kazuha Saionji, I think three rounds should suffice, hee-hee!
297:{character:player} I wasn't expecting a game of luck.
298:{character:Kaguyahime} Being blessed by the gods is also a kind of strength, mortal!
299:???
300:Kaguyahime
301:{character:player} The left tile.
302:{character:Kaguyahime} Allow me to have a look... Wow—congratulations! It's White!
303:{character:player} ...Isn't that a loss?
304:{character:Kaguyahime} Tee-hee! But you won a layer of protection, no? After all, the less you know, the safer you are, hmm?
305:{character:player} The right tile.
306:{character:Kaguyahime} Ah, I knew I was right to favor you, hee-hee!
308:{character:Kaguyahime} Now that I think about it, Four Greats each has their very own Mahjong dojo. If {var:player_nickname} really wants to approach them, perhaps it's safer to start from here, hee-hee!
309:{character:player} Please don't say that in such a weird way. It'll make people think I have ulterior motives.
310:{character:Kaguyahime} Eh? Could it possibly be that I have misunderstood something? Are you not asking about them specifically because you DO have some motives?
313:Kaguyahime turns around and rearranges the tiles. When she turns back, her fan again shows two tiles facing down. Which one to choose this time?
314:{character:Kaguyahime} It seems you're not nearly devout enough to me, so no luck this time. It's White, hee-hee!
315:{character:player} ...I'll get it next time.
316:{character:Kaguyahime} While I am willing to honor my promise, do you really wish to know, {var:player_nickname}?
317:{character:player} Yes.
318:{character:Kaguyahime} Very well then. Do you know where the largest convent in One Han City is?
319:{character:player} Where?
320:{character:Kaguyahime} In the northern suburbs. If you were to start walking there right now, you'd be there by... dusk.
321:{character:player} I appreciate your faith in me, but I don't think I'd be able to make it even by midnight. My human body can't walk solidly for six or seven hours...
322:{character:Kaguyahime} Ohoo! Humans really are so weak, hee-hee! But know that one of the Four Greats is there, a nun by the name of Lily Kitahara. I hear she has quite a lot of followers, many of whom will happily travel half the city to see her. But, if you want to talk about the number of followers, there's no way I'm losing out to some trifling nun!
323:{character:Kaguyahime} Right, {var:player_nickname}, my most faithful follower?
324:{character:player} Sure, whatever you say, O divine one.
325:{character:Kaguyahime} I knew there was a reason I favored you!
326:{character:Kaguyahime} Now, mortal... Your final chance!
327:Kaguyahime turns around once more, then presents me with the fan with the two tiles facing down. My last chance... Better make the most of it...
328:{character:Kaguyahime} Ohoo! Didn't your horoscope tell you that "left" is a big no-no today? Tee-hee, it's White!
329:{character:player} How can someone really not change positions three times in a row...?!
330:{character:Kaguyahime} How can someone really think that positions will change each time?
331:{character:Kaguyahime} Seeing as it's the final round, I suppose I can give you a little something for free!
332:{character:Kaguyahime} Fuuka Minami, the owner of the "Bamboo Cloud" business empire. It is said that she started out in catering. She owns a big chunk of One Han City's catering businesses, hee-hee!
333:{character:player} Is this what Saturne meant by fellow business person?
334:{character:Kaguyahime} Oh, it appears as though you have other sources of information! I may have underestimated you.
335:{character:player} A new friend of mine mentioned that one of the Four Greats was works in business.
336:{character:Kaguyahime} Oh? New friend?
337:{character:Kaguyahime} It's not like you suddenly have some new value that begs to be used. So I suppose that this new friend doesn't have any malicious motive. That's a relief, hee-hee! Mortal, come seek my blessing whenever you are in trouble, but don't forget the offerings.
