381:{character:Young Woman} Yes, it is a pity. This clearly would have been a match that can make everyone happy, eh—
382:{character:Wanjirou} You should thank {var:player_nickname}, Ichihime. You nearly fed another winner again.
383:{character:Ichihime} Nyaa? Why?
384:{character:Wanjirou} You wouldn't understand, anyway... But this lady's style reminds me of someone. I mean, such an odious playstyle is not very common, woof.
385:{character:player} Who?
386:{character:Wanjirou} Lily Kitahara, one of the Four Great Jyanshis. I've played with her before, and she'd also rely on this "feeding" strategy to get the best of her opponents. Back then the other player was just like Ichihime, foolishly thinking that she was a good person, playing just the tiles she needed, ahh—
387:{character:Ichihime} Nyaa! No personal attacks!
388:{character:player} Hmm... It is quite a coincidence that their styles are so similar.
389:{character:Wanjirou} It's not necessarily a coincidence. As one of the Four Greats, Lily Kitahara runs Boreas Dojo, one of the seven major dojos. Many admirers go there to learn from her, and picking up a trick or two like this isn't that hard.
390:{character:Wanjirou} Anyway, that young woman was far less devious than Lily Kitahara, and only someone like Ichihime, who doesn't even think about her hand, would take the bait like that, woof.
391:{character:Ichihime} Why are you belaboring the point, Wanjirou? Do you want a thump? Nyaa nyaa nyaaaa! Master, Ichihime is furious, NYAA!
392:{character:player} I'll go get you some cookies in a minute! Now... I had no idea that the Four Greats would be so different than how I imagined, that they'd be... Well, such pranksters.
393:{character:Wanjirou} The Four Greats are still people, after all, and there's no escaping from human nature. Anyway, why were you looking for me earlier?
394:{character:player} Umm... I'm looking for someone called Lily.
395:{character:Wanjirou} Isn't this Lily Kitahara? Even though she's clearly younger here, if you look closely her features are pretty similar.
396:{character:player} But the person who gave me the photo said her name was Lily D'Harques.
397:{character:Wanjirou} I can't speak to what happened in the past, but I'm certain she changed her name after becoming one of the Four Greats. Only she knows the real reason, woof.
398:{character:player} Seeing as you know her, do you also know where she lives now?
399:{character:Wanjirou} Let me give you an address.
400:{character:Wanjirou} The whole world knows your hand is in Tenpai, Ichihime, woof.
401:{character:Ichihime} So what, nyaa!
402:{character:Ichihime} Nyaa... I don't wanna play anymore nyaa... Why is it always me...
403:{character:Wanjirou} Because you're too greedy.
404:{character:Young Woman} My time's up too. I need to go. I look forward to playing with you all next time!
405:{character:player} Wanjirou, take a look at this. Do you have any impression of the blonde girl? She should be a bit older now, after all this photo is taken over a decade old.
406:{character:Wanjirou} Isn't this Lily Kitahara? Even though she's clearly younger here, if you look closely her features are pretty similar.
407:{character:player} Lily Kitahara?
408:{character:Wanjirou} Yeah. Lily Kitahara, one of the Four Great Jyanshis. Though I seem to recall a different name when she first came to the shrine. D... De...
409:{character:player} Lily D'Harques.
410:{character:Wanjirou} I don't really remember, but I think it was something like that. Why are you looking for her? That woman is not the easiest to deal with...
411:{character:player} We're not the ones looking for her. It's an old friend of hers, who's come a really long way to One Han City just to find her.
412:{character:Wanjirou} That woman's friend... Can't play as monstrously as her, surely...
413:{character:player} Um, well... As it happens I've never played with her. But for the couple of days I've known her, she's a lovely, lively woman. Presumably her playstyle would match her personality.
414:{character:Wanjirou} Anyway, if you're looking for Lily Kitahara, it shouldn't be hard to find her. Maybe you were having trouble finding her before because not many people know she changed her name.
415:{character:player} So, do you know where she lives these days?
416:{character:Wanjirou} Well, she's a nun, isn't she? So of course she's in a convent. Let me jot down the address.
417:{character:Kaguyahime} Very well, the game is over. Look, am I not fair? Guessed right, I told you. Guessed wrong, I did not. Tee-hee, how could I possibly trick anyone?!
418:{character:player} Well, great deity, what if I want to know more about the tournament?
419:{character:Kaguyahime} Hush, mortal—that will command a different price. And one which you can ill afford at present, hee-hee!
420:{character:player} How about a little discount?
421:{character:Ichihime} Do you want to take part in the Mahjong tournament, {var:player_nickname}?
422:{character:player} What makes you suddenly ask that?
423:{character:Kaguyahime} Oh midget, can you not see that {var:player_nickname} isn't interested? Why not ask me?
424:{character:player} Or...
425:{character:Kaguyahime} Your ice cream is melting, {var:player_nickname}.
426:{character:player} Oh oh oh oh!!
427:{character:Kaguyahime} In that case... Good luck, mortal!
428:{character:Kaguyahime} It's best if I take your place in the tournament. As for this food... Well, if you're not back in five minutes, there won't be anything left to eat.
474:I can't help but applaud Chiori's wit. Momo, standing at the side, isn't too sure what happened but joins in the applause anyway. Only Hinata stands in a huff, hands on hips.
475:{character:Kaguyahime} However, this is not important. Come, choose again. Let my divine self see how lucky you are, you who have long had my favor.
476:{character:player} If... Curiosity is also an aim...
477:{character:Kaguyahime} Let me think about who should I tell you first... Ah, Kurone Toujou, she's the manager of the Geisha House "Countless Springs", and the most famous geisha in all of One Han City. She's also in charge of one of the city's seven major dojos...
